      "message": "Hrm. I\u0027m not super familiar with the BTF details here, but I\u0027d think MODULE_ALLOW_BTF_MISMATCH would allow the mali_kbase.ko to load.  Could you add some debug prints around the logic where the \"mali_kbase: disagrees about version of symbol module_layout\" error crops up?\n\nOn the hikey issue, I really don\u0027t have much of a guess right off, as it seems like its not even getting to the kernel. Hrm. I wonder if the config is growing the kernel size past some of the bootloader\u0027s internal limits? Maybe hikey needs an update for something like: https://github.com/96boards-hikey/edk2/commit/53a99b7e4f39a4dcf5b6a828ee6a49be18c1b0ac\n\nLets move this hikey discussion to a separate email thread, but keep the hikey960 issue here for now.",
